Description: MeshSat node and pocket Bridge for the PinePhone LoRa back cover
 Makes a PinePhone or PinePhone Pro with the Pine64 LoRa back cover a
 Meshtastic node (Meshtastic's Linux daemon with the MeshSat bridge layer
 for the cover's ATtiny I2C-to-SPI bridge), runs the MeshSat Bridge beside
 it over TCP, and puts the Bridge's interface in a phone-sized app with an
 icon in the app grid. A watchdog tells the user when the radio stopped
 answering and the cover must be re-seated, and starts the node again when
 it answers.
 .
 Pre-release. The radio in the cover is qualified at 0 dBm only (a plain
 crystal that drifts as the amplifier heats); range at that power is a
 house or a street. Built for Debian 13 (Mobian) on arm64.
